// expect: refuse E_MissingVariable
// AN EFFECT NAME IN A ROW RESOLVES OR REFUSES. A `with` term that names no
// effect declared in the module's reach — no `effect Nowhere` anywhere this
// module links — is E_MissingVariable at the declaration. Until Landing 1
// (2026-10-13) the expansion took an unknown name as an effect OF THAT NAME,
// so the clause checked clean and constrained nothing: lib/persist.mn's
// `!Network` held two weeks after the last Network effect left the tree on
// 2026-09-28. Measured on boot 454c3aaf: this program compiled clean and ran
// to 1.
fn quiet() with !Nowhere = 1

fn main() = quiet()
